#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Phase 3 - Module: :NameRecord / :NameVariant   (via-reification, SELF-CONTAINED)

Runs a SPARQL CONSTRUCT against Fuseki and writes the ontology-grounded triples as Turtle.

SELF-CONTAINED (user request, 2026-09-08) - mirrors participant_role.py / temporal_extent.py /
description.py / external_reference.py. This module emits ONLY triples whose SUBJECT is a class it
owns (:NameRecord or its minted :NameVariant nodes). A link whose subject is some OTHER entity is a
fact about that entity, so it is RE-HOMED to that entity's module and NOT emitted here:
  * ?agent :hasNameRecord ?nr   -> a fact about the Agent (hasNameRecord ⊑ hasAgentRecord); belongs
    to the Agent module, which consumes these :NameRecord nodes and asserts the owning edge. agent.py
    currently DEFERS its hasAgentRecord-subproperty edges (agent memory D-AG-1), so this edge is
    emitted there when that work lands. Until then the owner-of-record (V6, and :NameRecord's
    inverse(hasAgentRecord) card-1) is satisfied only with agent.ttl co-loaded - the same vacuous-
    until-co-loaded check the other self-contained modules carry.
:recordedAt, :isDirectlyBasedOn, :hasTemporalExtent and the :hasNameVariant/:hasPreferredNameVariant
edges all have the RECORD as subject, so they STAY - they are the record's own facts.

WHY VIA-REIFICATION (diagnostics 2026-08-23, decision reversed from the first plan)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The plan filed NameRecord as a SYNTHESIS module and mapping-properties-reconciled.csv /
coverage-gaps.csv both said :fullNameAsString has "no wiki source found". The Step-0 diagnostics
(name_record_diagnostics.rq E2/E6b/E7) show that is WRONG:

  * edt:P20 (hasName) sits on 719,545 of 732,352 persons (98.2%) - persons DO carry P20, contrary
    to agent_diagnostics E3b's guess. P20 IS the full-name source (E2).
  * The per-name fact is REIFIED: ep:P20 -> 721,624 statement nodes (E6b), one per name, carrying
    qualifiers - pq:P18 recordedAt on 705,559 and prov:wasDerivedFrom on 721,623 (E7).

So, exactly as age_record.py did for P42, the STATEMENT node IS the :NameRecord. Its IRI already
exists and is stable, so nothing is minted for the record; eps:P20 gives the required
:fullNameAsString and the qualifiers fill two INHERITED AgentRecord slots (:recordedAt,
:isDirectlyBasedOn) that a synthesised record would have left empty. This corroborates the prior
(deleted) session's ~722,984 figure = 721,624 person + ~1,360 org P20 statements.

CRITICAL - AGENT TYPE GUARD
  P20 hasName is SHARED: it is native to Event and Place too (event.py already renames it to
  :hasName for Events). Without the `?agent edt:P1 (Q410|Q411)` guard, every Event/Place name
  statement would be turned into a :NameRecord. The guard is what scopes P20 to agents here.

MOVES
  DE-REIFY  ?agent ep:P20 ?nr                    -> the statement node becomes :NameRecord
  VALUE     ?nr eps:P20 ?fullName                 -> :fullNameAsString  (card 1, xsd:string)
  QUALIFIER ?nr pq:P18 ?event                     -> :recordedAt        (max 1, -> :Event)
  EXTENT    ?nr pq:P18 ?event (event dated P28/P63)-> :hasTemporalExtent <event>-extent (card 1)
                                                     reuses temporal_extent.py's node IRI; link only
                                                     when the extent node exists (nodes-only module).
  PROVENANCE ?nr prov:wasDerivedFrom ?ref ; ?ref epr:P6 ?source
                                                  -> :isDirectlyBasedOn ?source (max 1)  [EWP D-EWP-2]
  PART      ?agent edt:P73 ?firstName             -> :hasFirstNameAsString (max 1)   (DEC-2: P73=first)
  PART      ?agent edt:P72 ?surname               -> :hasSurnameAsString   (max 1)   (DEC-2: P72=surname)
  VARIANT   only when the agent has ALTERNATE name(s) (P71) - a "multiple names" record:
            mint <nr>-pref a :NameVariant ; rdfs:label ?fullName -> :hasPreferredNameVariant + :hasNameVariant
            mint <nr>-nv-<md5(alt)> a :NameVariant ; rdfs:label ?altName (per P71 alt) -> :hasNameVariant
            A SINGLE-name record (no P71) gets NO variant at all.
  RE-HOMED  ?agent :hasNameRecord ?nr  -> NOT emitted here (SELF-CONTAINED, above); the Agent module
            asserts this owning edge. ?agent is still bound in WHERE (guard + name parts), just not
            used as an emitted subject.

DEC-2 (P72/P73 direction), settled by E5: the sample reads P73="James"/"Richard"/"John" (given
names), P72="Alexander"/"Baker"/"Bayard" (family names), label = "P73 P72". The mapping is CORRECT
as written - P73 -> firstname, P72 -> surname. NOT inverted (the deleted memory's claim was wrong).
E5b's label-prefix vote confirms it quantitatively: 239,183 labels start with P73 vs 930 with P72
(2026-09-08 run). (An earlier FILTER-only-OPTIONAL E5b returned 0/0 - a portability bug, since fixed.)

ACCEPTED MULTIPLICITY (DEC-4, logged not silently fixed - the age_record.py precedent)
  P73/P72/P71 are direct on the AGENT, not on the name statement, so a person with >1 name
  statement (1,237, E4) has their parts attached to EACH record; a person with >1 P73 (938) or
  >1 P72 (884) yields a record with 2 first/surnames -> a max-1 violation. Some pq:P18 statements
  carry 2 recordedAt (817,931 P18 uses over 721,624 statements, E6). All are REAL source
  multiplicity - emitted as-is, surfaced by Phase-5 SHACL, never arbitrarily picked.

SCOPE (DEC-5): guard is VALUES { ed:Q410 ed:Q411 } - Persons AND Organizations. Orgs carry P20
  (all 1,354, E2b) but essentially no parts (2 have P72), so an org record is fullName + preferred
  variant. Restrict to ed:Q410 alone to make this Person-only.

VARIANTS ARE MULTI-NAME-ONLY (user rule, 2026-08-23)
  A record whose agent has no P71 alternate name is a SINGLE name: it gets NO :NameVariant and no
  :hasPreferredNameVariant (its name is on :fullNameAsString alone). Only a "multiple names" agent
  (>=1 P71) gets a variant set - the primary as preferred, each alternate as a variant. This
  RELAXES :NameRecord's `hasNameVariant someValuesFrom :NameVariant` (min 1) to fire only on
  multi-name records; a Phase-5 ontology call (relax the restriction to min 0), logged like
  Event's hasExternalReference min-1. Most records (P71 is on only 39,275/732,352 persons) have
  no variant by design - do not read that as a defect.

HAS-TEMPORAL-EXTENT (wired 2026-09-08, decision settled - supersedes the old "TBD / not emitted here")
  temporal_extent.py became NODES-ONLY (it emits the :TemporalExtent/:TimeSpan node but NOT the
  `<subject> :hasTemporalExtent <extent>` link, since that link is a fact about the OWNING subject).
  So NameRecord - the owner - emits the link itself, over its :recordedAt event, reusing the SAME
  deterministic <event>-extent IRI that module mints. A dedicated OPTIONAL adds the property-path
  guard `?recordedAtEvent edt:P28|edt:P63 ?extentDate` (the exact condition for an <event>-extent node
  to exist), then binds ?temporalExtent = <event>-extent; emitted ONLY for dated recordedAt events,
  so no link dangles. This OPTIONAL is SEPARATE from the :recordedAt one, so an undated recordedAt
  event still keeps :recordedAt while staying extent-bare (the accepted gap AgeRecord carries). To
  verify the objects resolve to real typed extents, co-load temporal_extent.ttl with name_record.ttl
  (see V9). Same property-path shape as participant_role.py; the AgeRecord "query B", re-homed here.

EMPTY / GAP BY DESIGN (confirmed, not missed)
  * ~12,807 persons have an rdfs:label but NO P20 statement (E1-E2), so they get NO record here.
    Their name lives only in the label. Documented coverage gap (log to coverage-gaps.csv); a
    label-only synthesis fallback is possible if full coverage is wanted - deliberately NOT added,
    to keep this a pure de-reification pass like age_record.py.
  * typing ?event :Event / ?source provenance / ?agent :Person -> owned by those modules.
  * NO rdfs:label on the :NameRecord itself - the name lives on :fullNameAsString and on the
    preferred :NameVariant's label; a record is not a name (age_record discipline).

Usage (from repo root, Fuseki serving the dump):
    python src/phase3/name_record.py --dataset Enslaved-dataset                # full run
    python src/phase3/name_record.py --dataset Enslaved-dataset --test          # one agent
    python src/phase3/name_record.py --dataset Enslaved-dataset --iri ed:Q1124931 --test
    python src/phase3/name_record.py --limit 100
    python src/phase3/name_record.py --print-query
Writes out/phase3/name_record.ttl. Standard library only.
"""

import argparse
import os
import sys
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
from paths import OUT_PHASE3, ensure  # noqa: E402

# A known Person carrying P20 + P73 + P72 (E5: "James Alexander").
TEST_ENTITY = "ed:Q1124931"

CONSTRUCT = """
PREFIX :        <https://enslaved.org/ontology/>
PREFIX ed:      <https://lod.enslaved.org/entity/>
PREFIX edt:     <https://lod.enslaved.org/prop/direct/>
PREFIX ep:      <https://lod.enslaved.org/prop/>
PREFIX eps:     <https://lod.enslaved.org/prop/statement/>
PREFIX pq:      <https://lod.enslaved.org/prop/qualifier/>
PREFIX epr:     <https://lod.enslaved.org/prop/reference/>
PREFIX prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
PREFIX wikibase:<http://wikiba.se/ontology#>
PREFIX rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

CONSTRUCT {{
    ?nr  a   :NameRecord ;
         :fullNameAsString        ?fullName ;
         :hasFirstNameAsString    ?firstName ;
         :hasSurnameAsString      ?surname ;
         :recordedAt              ?recordedAtEvent ;
         :hasTemporalExtent       ?temporalExtent ;
         :isDirectlyBasedOn       ?source ;
         :hasPreferredNameVariant ?prefVar ;
         :hasNameVariant          ?prefVar , ?altVar .
    ?prefVar a :NameVariant ; rdfs:label ?fullName .
    ?altVar  a :NameVariant ; rdfs:label ?altName .
}}
WHERE {{
    {values}
    # AGENT GUARD - P20 is also Event/Place's name; without this, their name statements would
    # become :NameRecords. Drop ed:Q411 below to restrict to Persons only (DEC-5).
    ?agent edt:P1 ?agentClass .
    VALUES ?agentClass {{ ed:Q410 ed:Q411 }}

    ?agent ep:P20  ?nr .                        # reified "has name"  => the record node
    ?nr    eps:P20 ?fullName .                   # the full name string => :fullNameAsString (card 1)

    # deprecated statements are retracted claims - do not materialise them
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {{ ?nr wikibase:rank wikibase:DeprecatedRank }}

    # :recordedAt - statement qualifier (max 1, inherited AgentRecord slot). Bound in its OWN
    # OPTIONAL, independent of dating, so every record with pq:P18 keeps :recordedAt even when its
    # event is undated (~705,559 of 722,984 stmts carry pq:P18).
    OPTIONAL {{ ?nr pq:P18 ?recordedAtEvent . }}

    # :hasTemporalExtent - REUSE the recordedAt event's temporal_extent.py <event>-extent node. That
    # module is NODES-ONLY (emits the extent node, never the <subject> :hasTemporalExtent link), so
    # NameRecord - the owner - emits the link. The property-path guard `edt:P28|edt:P63 ?extentDate`
    # is the exact condition an <event>-extent node exists (TE=P28, TS=P28+P63, EO=P63), so the link
    # never dangles; undated recordedAt events stay extent-bare (accepted gap, like AgeRecord). Kept
    # a SEPARATE OPTIONAL from :recordedAt above (do NOT fold the date requirement into that one, or
    # undated events lose :recordedAt). Same ?recordedAtEvent var: for a record with several
    # recordedAt events this binds the extent only on the dated one(s), leaving the others' :recordedAt
    # intact. A multi-date event matches once per date -> duplicate rows binding the SAME
    # ?temporalExtent (and an unused ?extentDate); CONSTRUCT dedups. Mirrors participant_role.py.
    OPTIONAL {{
        ?nr pq:P18 ?recordedAtEvent .
        ?recordedAtEvent edt:P28|edt:P63 ?extentDate .
        BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(?recordedAtEvent), "-extent")) AS ?temporalExtent)
    }}

    # :isDirectlyBasedOn - a REFERENCE-level fact (EntityWithProvenance D-EWP-2), reached by
    # walking the statement's reference node ONE MORE HOP to its epr:P6 source. prov:wasDerivedFrom
    # alone stops at the reference node (edref:...), which is the citation WRAPPER, not the source;
    # the actual source document is `?ref epr:P6 ?source`. (P6 lives only on reference nodes -
    # 0 direct / 0 statement-value, per EWP E1-E3 - so this two-hop walk is the only route.)
    OPTIONAL {{ ?nr prov:wasDerivedFrom ?ref . ?ref epr:P6 ?source . }}

    # name parts: DIRECT claims on the agent (not on the statement). Attached to the record via
    # the agent; for a multi-name agent this attaches to each record (DEC-4, accepted).
    OPTIONAL {{ ?agent edt:P73 ?firstName . }}   # DEC-2: P73 = first name
    OPTIONAL {{ ?agent edt:P72 ?surname . }}     # DEC-2: P72 = surname

    # VARIANTS ONLY WHEN THE AGENT HAS MULTIPLE NAMES (user rule, 2026-08-23). A single-name agent
    # (no P71 alternate) gets NO :NameVariant and NO :hasPreferredNameVariant - the lone name lives
    # only on :fullNameAsString. When the agent DOES carry alternate name(s), the record gets the
    # primary full name as the PREFERRED variant (<nr>-pref) plus one variant per alternate
    # (<nr>-nv-<md5(alt)>). This deliberately RELAXES the ontology's :hasNameVariant someValuesFrom
    # (min 1) to "only for multi-name records" - logged like Event's hasExternalReference min-1.
    #
    # CRITICAL (bug found in the first full run, 2026-09-08): the ?prefVar/?altVar BINDs must sit at
    # OUTER scope, NOT inside the P71 OPTIONAL. A BIND that references ?nr (bound in the ENCLOSING
    # group) from INSIDE the OPTIONAL evaluates to UNBOUND in both Jena and rdflib - the same
    # outer-variable-in-OPTIONAL scoping trap as the old E5b FILTER-BIND bug - so the first run
    # emitted ZERO variants (V4/V7 = 0) even though 39,275 agents carry P71. Fix: the OPTIONAL only
    # MATCHES the alternate (binds ?altName), then the IRIs are minted OUTSIDE it where ?nr is in
    # scope, guarded by IF(BOUND(?altName), <iri>, ?unbound) - unbound (=no variant) for single-name
    # records, the multi-name-only rule. This mirrors the extent IF idiom above.
    OPTIONAL {{ ?agent edt:P71 ?altName . }}
    BIND(IF(BOUND(?altName), IRI(CONCAT(STR(?nr), "-pref")), ?unboundPref) AS ?prefVar)
    BIND(IF(BOUND(?altName), IRI(CONCAT(STR(?nr), "-nv-", MD5(STR(?altName)))), ?unboundAlt) AS ?altVar)
}}
{limit}
"""


def build_query(test: bool, iri: str, limit) -> str:
    values = f"VALUES ?agent {{ {iri} }}" if test else ""
    limit_clause = f"LIMIT {limit}" if limit else ""
    return CONSTRUCT.format(values=values, limit=limit_clause)


def count_triples(ttl: str) -> int:
    """Rough triple count = ',' ';' '.' separators OUTSIDE quoted literals (agent.py heuristic).

    RIOT packs multi-valued objects inline as 'a , b' and writes ';' with no leading space, so
    counting the separators (skipping those inside string literals, e.g. commas in a name) is
    closer than a line-suffix count. Approximate but honest.
    """
    n = 0
    for raw in ttl.splitlines():
        s = raw.lstrip()
        if not s or s.startswith(("@", "#", "PREFIX")):
            continue
        in_quote = escaped = False
        for ch in raw:
            if escaped:
                escaped = False
            elif ch == "\\":
                escaped = True
            elif ch == '"':
                in_quote = not in_quote
            elif not in_quote and ch in ",;.":
                n += 1
    return n


def run_construct(endpoint: str, query: str) -> str:
    """POST a CONSTRUCT query; return Turtle."""
    data = urllib.parse.urlencode({"query": query}).encode("utf-8")
    req = urllib.request.Request(
        endpoint,
        data=data,
        headers={
            "Accept": "text/turtle",
            "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded",
        },
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:
        return resp.read().decode("utf-8")


def main() -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Phase 3 :NameRecord CONSTRUCT (via-reification of ep:P20).")
    ap.add_argument("--server", default="http://localhost:3030")
    ap.add_argument("--dataset", default="Enslaved-dataset")
    ap.add_argument("--test", action="store_true",
                    help=f"restrict to one agent ({TEST_ENTITY}, or --iri) for a shape check")
    ap.add_argument("--iri", default=TEST_ENTITY,
                    help=f"agent IRI for --test (default {TEST_ENTITY})")
    ap.add_argument("--limit", type=int, default=None,
                    help="cap solutions (smoke-test a slice of the ~723k statements)")
    ap.add_argument("--out", default=None,
                    help="output .ttl path (default out/phase3/name_record.ttl)")
    ap.add_argument("--print-query", action="store_true", help="print generated SPARQL and exit")
    args = ap.parse_args()

    query = build_query(args.test, args.iri, args.limit)
    if args.print_query:
        print(query)
        return 0

    endpoint = f"{args.server.rstrip('/')}/{args.dataset}/query"
    out_path = args.out or os.path.join(ensure(OUT_PHASE3), "name_record.ttl")

    scope = f"TEST: {args.iri} only" if args.test else "full run"
    if args.limit:
        scope += f", LIMIT {args.limit}"
    print(f"Querying {endpoint}  ({scope})")

    ttl = run_construct(endpoint, query)
    with open(out_path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(ttl)

    print(f"wrote {out_path}  (~{count_triples(ttl)} triples, {len(ttl.encode('utf-8'))} bytes)")

    if args.test:
        print(f"--- expected shape for {args.iri} (if it is a Q410/Q411 carrying P20) ---")
        print("  SINGLE-name agent (no P71) - e.g. ed:Q1124931 'James Alexander':")
        print("  (SELF-CONTAINED: the <agent> :hasNameRecord <stmt> edge is RE-HOMED to the Agent")
        print("   module and is NOT in this output - the record's own facts only:)")
        print("    <stmt> a :NameRecord ;")
        print('        :fullNameAsString "James Alexander" ;')
        print('        :hasFirstNameAsString "James" ; :hasSurnameAsString "Alexander" ;')
        print("        :recordedAt ed:… ; :isDirectlyBasedOn <the SOURCE, not the edref: node> ;")
        print("        :hasTemporalExtent <recordedAt-event>-extent  (ONLY if that event has P28/P63) .")
        print("    (NO :NameVariant / :hasPreferredNameVariant - single name, by the multi-name rule)")
        print("  MULTI-name agent (>=1 P71 alternate): additionally")
        print("    <stmt> :hasPreferredNameVariant <stmt>-pref ; :hasNameVariant <stmt>-pref , <stmt>-nv-… .")
        print('    <stmt>-pref a :NameVariant ; rdfs:label "<full name>" .')
        print('    <stmt>-nv-<md5> a :NameVariant ; rdfs:label "<alternate name>" .')
        print("  TIP: to see a multi-name record, pass an --iri with a P71, e.g. find one via")
        print("    SELECT ?s { ?s edt:P1 ed:Q410 ; edt:P71 [] } LIMIT 1")
    else:
        print("Checks (run name_record_diagnostics.py --phase after, with name_record.ttl loaded):")
        print("  V1: ~722,984 :NameRecord (721,624 person + ~1,360 org P20 statements, E6b);")
        print("  V2: :fullNameAsString EXACTLY 1 per record (0 with none / 0 with multi);")
        print("  V3: :hasFirstNameAsString / :hasSurnameAsString max 1 (== E4 multis, DEC-4);")
        print("  V4: :NameVariant tracks MULTI-name only - records_with_variant ~= agents with P71;")
        print("      single-name records with no variant are EXPECTED and large, not a defect;")
        print("  V5: :hasPreferredNameVariant max 1 (0 violations);")
        print("  V6 (needs agent.ttl): SELF-CONTAINED - :hasNameRecord is emitted by the Agent module,")
        print("      NOT here, so this is vacuous vs output-only; co-load agent.ttl to check owner+type;")
        print("  V7: no dangling variants - every :hasNameVariant object typed :NameVariant + labelled.")
        print("  V9: :hasTemporalExtent now emitted here over dated recordedAt events (was 0); its")
        print("      objects are <event>-extent IRIs - co-load temporal_extent.ttl to confirm they type.")
        print("  GAP (E1-E2): ~12,807 label-only persons get no record; records whose recordedAt")
        print("      event is undated stay extent-bare (accepted gap, like AgeRecord).")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
